Z||000000||Ferrari_cdn||07-12-2001||11:07 PM||||I am planning on purchasing a '84 Fiero from my brother in law's uncle who lives in BC, and I'm here in Winnipeg.  I saw your info so I thought I'll ask you how your Fiero handles in the winter.   Such as, how well can you control it in the snow and how well does it heat up the car after starting it out in the cold?  I'm asking you since I know that you know how damn cold it can be sometimes!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000001||Mach10||07-13-2001||01:48 AM||||Welcome in! I replied to your other post, as I saw it first. <BR>I don't have a whole lot of experience in the winter. <BR>That said, I have driven enough to have a feel for the car. First, it's got great traction. Wide tires, weight over driveaxles. Rear-drive means you have to be careful about throttle in corners. Keep speed constant. Coasting will send your back end out, as will flooring it. Stopping is no worse than any other car on ice... All in all, it feels fine, but you need to watch your back end. Mid-engined means that once that ass starts to swing, it has a lot of momentum, and wants to keep swinging. Take it easy, and I've found that it's almost as nice as FWD. That's the key. Take it easy.<P>Oh, by the way, if you're interested in a local Fiero, I know a guy that will hook you up in no time. He always has 2 or 3 of 'em for sale. Him and his friend the bodyshop guy restore the things. Is this the same guy as your brother in-law's friend? ||||reg||6
Z||000002||baldlobo||07-13-2001||01:52 AM||||welcome to the club, nice to see another 'peg other than mach10. oh, yeah I've got a red 84, that's in need of minor repair(haven't gotten to drive it yet) you should really put up a post to attract the attention of Overlord; he drive's his all year round and lives outside winnipeg.<p>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ferrari_cdn||07-13-2001||02:15 AM||||I'll ask him for the name of his friend.<P>It's so funny about Fieros, because the story is like this:<P>I've never known Fieros until now.  A week ago when my bro in law, Steve S., told me about a Fiero, then I looked it up on the web.  Then on my way home driving from work, I thought about seeing a Fiero while driving.  I got frustrated not seeing one when I stopped at a red light on Portage.  A car in front of me happens to be a gray Fiero GT.  lol.<P>Then today, I stopped at Safeway (Henderson and Kimberly), to pick up a Computer Paper.  Saw a red '84 (I think) Fiero parked at the corner by the intersection, and it was for sale.  I jotted down the number just in case.<BR>Then tonight I went back to the bank at that same intersection to get some money, walked out and saw a yellow Fiero turning onto Henderson from Kimberly.<P>It's weird, seeing a lot of them just as I learned about it.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Ferrari_cdn (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||k2m4||07-13-2001||10:01 AM||||Hey Ferrari_cdn<BR>i posted something about fieros in the winter in your other thread. Like i said there my car is the best winter car ive ever driven see my other post<P>kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||TRiAD||07-13-2001||10:25 AM||||I can't speak for Fiero yet, but I would think they would be similar in the snow to an MR2, and I have driven many of those...<BR>With the MR layout, the engine is basically over and in front of the rear axles, so the grip is better than any front-engined layout I can think of. MR2s are better in the snow than many cars in the dry. I'm sure Fieros are about the same. <BR>Welcome and good luck!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||07-14-2001||11:05 AM||||Hey Ferrari_cdn!<BR>I have driven my 84 Fiero in the winter for 13 years, so it can be done, BUT, the floor is rusted out now...<BR>Now I don't drive my 86 in the winter...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
